  "_comment": "Bytes are 0x-hex, lower case; inside a file's text (envelope, item, header) bytes are base64 (RFC 4648 §4, padded). Generated by clients/clientkeys/scripts/profile-vectors.mjs (src/profile.js); never edit by hand. Random inputs are fixed: rnd(name, n) = the first n bytes of keccak256(\"scaas/profile/vectors/<name>/0\") ‖ keccak256(\"scaas/profile/vectors/<name>/1\") ‖ …; the labels are in the generator. Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-27-user-profiles.md (§4, §6, §7.1, §7.2, §10.1) and the plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-27-user-profiles.md (\"Pinned formats\"). UNAUDITED. export.json: the file = \"SCAASPX1\" ‖ be32(header_len) ‖ header ‖ chunks; chunk_i = AES-256-GCM-SIV(K_x, nonce_prefix ‖ be32(i) ‖ last_i, AD_i = lp(scaas.profile-export) ‖ be32(header_len) ‖ header ‖ be32(i), 1 MiB of payload each, the last 1 to 1 MiB); K_x = HKDF-SHA256(Argon2id(OpaqueString(passphrase)), salt empty, info \"scaas.profile-export.v1\"); payload = be32(len) ‖ label JSON ‖ be32(len) ‖ settings ‖ be16(count) ‖ (lp(name) ‖ be32(len) ‖ bytes)*. headers at both sets; keys; files at the test set (under test-hooks): small (the whole file) and 1 MiB, 1 MiB + 1, 2 MiB of payload whose keystore item is the filler rnd(<filler>, <len>), recorded by length, SHA-256, chunk count, first and last 64 bytes. refusals: each is ProfileImportOpen with its local reason; the file is `file`, or `base` with `edit` (truncate n: drop the last n bytes; replace offset hex; drop_chunk i; swap_chunks i j; append_chunk i: a copy of chunk i at the end; chunks are 1,048,592 bytes from 12 + header_len; null: the base as is), or `file_len` bytes of zeros led by `prefix_bytes`; size_control: the length bound itself passes the length check.",
